import{_ as t,o as s,c as o,a0 as n}from"./chunks/framework.D4fUSYzX.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"ADR 0137: The mutation campaign host runs the vendored typescript shim","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/0137-the-mutation-campaign-host-runs-the-vendored-typescript-shim.md","filePath":"adr/0137-the-mutation-campaign-host-runs-the-vendored-typescript-shim.md"}'),a={name:"adr/0137-the-mutation-campaign-host-runs-the-vendored-typescript-shim.md"};function r(i,e,c,h,d,p){return s(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="adr-0137-the-mutation-campaign-host-runs-the-vendored-typescript-shim" tabindex="-1">ADR 0137: The mutation campaign host runs the vendored typescript shim <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0137-the-mutation-campaign-host-runs-the-vendored-typescript-shim" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR 0137: The mutation campaign host runs the vendored typescript shim&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Status: accepted Date: 2026-10-13 Amends ADR 0055&#39;s campaign setup on one point of the host, not of the campaign: the Stryker process resolves a vendored copy of the one typescript function its ts-config preprocessor reads, so the campaign starts on the typescript 7.0.2 this repository declares. The suite, the scope, and the thresholds ADR 0055 fixed stand untouched.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The campaign&#39;s host process runs Stryker core on the Bun runtime. One part of the host reads the repository&#39;s typescript: core&#39;s ts-config preprocessor imports the bare specifier <code>typescript</code> from its own package and reads <code>parseConfigFileTextToJson</code> from it. That is the parse it runs on the sandbox copy&#39;s <code>tsconfig.json</code> before it rewrites the file&#39;s <code>extends</code>, <code>references</code>, <code>include</code>, <code>exclude</code>, and <code>files</code> paths for the sandbox, and the preprocessor runs before the campaign&#39;s scope is applied.</p><p>The typescript this repository declares is 7.0.2, the native compiler line <code>bun run typecheck</code> and the Quality audit run (ADR 0120, ADR 0121). That line exposes no compiler API: its entry stands on a version export and a compiler process, and <code>parseConfigFileTextToJson</code> is not among its exports. A host that resolves the top-level package therefore died at the campaign&#39;s first step with <code>ts.parseConfigFileTextToJson is not a function</code>, and scoping the campaign to a single file did not avoid it, because the preprocessor runs either way (issue #377): no campaign, scoped or full, could start.</p><p>No release answers the native line. Stryker 10.0.0, the latest on the registry, still reads the compiler API. And the declared version does not move: ADR 0120 and ADR 0121 line the Quality audit and the type check on the native line, and moving the repository&#39;s typescript to an older line to satisfy one plugin&#39;s import would move the type check and the audit with it.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The host resolves its own copy of the one function the preprocessor reads. The checkout vendors a shim, <code>scripts/stryker-host-typescript</code>: a package named <code>typescript</code> whose entry implements <code>parseConfigFileTextToJson</code> on a small JSONC parse - plain JSON plus the comments and trailing commas the real parse tolerates - and nothing else of the typescript API. <code>scripts/mutate.sh</code> stages the shim at <code>node_modules/@stryker-mutator/core/node_modules/typescript</code> before every run, where the preprocessor&#39;s import finds it before the top-level 7.0.2, and it re-stages on every run because <code>bun install</code> can prune a staged copy.</p><p>Bare-specifier resolution is per package, and the preprocessor is the only <code>typescript</code> reader in the host process: the instrumenter and the Bun runner plugin keep resolving the top-level line exactly as before. The declared typescript, the type check, and the Quality audit stand untouched, and the campaign measures the same suite, scope, and thresholds ADR 0055 fixed. The shim touches no part of the instrumentation, the run, or the score.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>A campaign starts on the typescript 7.0.2 the repository declares. The crash of issue #377 stands closed, and the scoped campaign over the Handoff dispatch and the observation runs on this branch; its score stands in the <a href="https://github.com/SeriousJul/my-little-software-factory/blob/main/docs/verification/mutation-testing.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mutation-testing record</a>.</li><li>The shim&#39;s surface is its contract. A Stryker release that reads more of the typescript API must widen the shim and its tests on purpose; the host never falls back to the native line, which carries no API to read.</li><li>The staging stands in <code>node_modules</code>, which <code>bun install</code> rebuilds. The entry point owns the re-stage, and it refuses a campaign whose checkout lost the shim, so a tree cannot start the host on the top-level line again silently.</li><li>The shim is not a compiler. It runs no type check and compiles nothing. It answers the one parse the preprocessor asks, and a tsconfig it cannot read answers <code>config: undefined</code>, the same answer the preprocessor gives a file it cannot rewrite.</li></ul>',11)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
